{"qid":"Q1014","names":["Republic of Liberia"],"title":"Republic of Liberia","endonym":{"native":"Republic of Liberia","lang":"en"},"capsule":"Liberia was established in 1847 as Africa's first republic by formerly enslaved African Americans repatriated under the auspices of the American Colonization Society, with Monrovia—named for U.S. President James Monroe—as its capital. The Americo-Liberian oligarchy dominated political life for over a century until Master Sergeant Samuel Doe's coup on 12 April 1980 ended True Whig Party rule; his authoritarian government in turn collapsed in a civil war from 1989, in which Doe was killed in 1990. A second civil war (1999–2003) devastated the country before the election of Ellen Johnson Sirleaf in 2005—Africa's first female head of state—inaugurated a period of reconstruction.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Modern Liberia's borders are well defined by treaty and are consistently mapped; 19th-century interior control was minimal and territorial claims often nominal.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Liberia","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Liberia"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Liberia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberia"},{"label":"Wikipedia: History of Liberia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Liberia"}],"britannica":"place/Liberia","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Liberia","rulers":[{"qid":"Q360164","name":"Joseph Jenkins Roberts","start":1848,"end":1856,"image":"Joseph Jenkins Roberts c. 1865 (A) (cropped).tif","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Joseph%20Jenkins%20Roberts%20c.%201865%20(A)%20(cropp